{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgdXnRCGxo2etoczGUHrp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Moonshot released Kimi K3.1 Pro on its API on October 23, and Artificial Analysis scored it 55. That puts it ahead of Claude Fable 5.1, GPT-6 Astra and Gemini 4 Argon, which all scored 53, and behind only Claude Opus 5.5 at 58. The article's author says this is the first time a model that will soon have open weights has scored this highly against the frontier.\n\nThe open-weights part is still a promise. The model is not yet downloadable, and Moonshot says \"Full model weights will be released by Nov 4, 2026.\" Until that happens, Kimi K3.1 Pro is available only through Moonshot's API.\n\nThe pricing is where the score becomes practical. Moonshot charges $2.00 per million input tokens and $10 per million output tokens. That matches GPT-6.1 Sol and is half the price of Claude Opus 5.5. Comparing the two figures, Opus 5.5 leads by three points on the Artificial Analysis scale at twice the cost. Whether three points justifies double the price depends on the workload, and the article does not say. There is also a \"Highspeed\" version that is 2-3x faster at twice the price, with input token cache hits priced the same as the standard version.\n\nThe benchmark claims come from different sources. Moonshot's own benchmarks show Kimi roughly level with Opus 5.5 and GPT-6 Astra, ahead on a few tests and close on others. That is the company's account, while the Artificial Analysis score is a separate comparison and the better evidence of where the model sits.\n\nThe author also tried the model through Moonshot's API, using the llm tool's openai endpoint command. They generated an SVG of a pelican riding a bicycle at the three reasoning levels Kimi supports (low, medium and max), and compared the results with fresh runs from Kimi K3. The excerpt shows no verdict from that comparison, so the independent score and Moonshot's benchmarks are the main evidence of quality so far."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2229,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2229},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1ec212ea-5e83-4866-b5f5-5669c9cacf73","uuid":"801f4dd1-5f38-431a-b865-fa01e78edeee","timestamp":"2026-11-02T05:15:06.275Z","request_id":"req_011CgdXnQyNnLV8szHCAhWCd"}
